      "raw_response": "ANSWER: SUPPORTED\n\nThe abstract directly supports the claim that AIRE is expressed in some skin tumors. It describes that autoimmune regulator (Aire), which is implicated in the regulation of gene expression, is upregulated in human and mouse tumor keratinocytes in a K17-dependent manner, contributing to the timely onset of skin tumorigenesis in mice. Furthermore, it mentions that K17 colocalizes with Aire protein in tumor-prone keratinocytes and that both factors are bound to specific promoter regions with NF-\u03baB consensus sequences in a relevant subset of genes. This suggests that Aire expression is linked to K17 expression and tumorigenesis in skin tissues. (Source: Nature Communications, 2021)",
